        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en"># Included processes\nElectricity from wind farm, fed to grid. Includes the operation of the wind farm with the necessary change of gear oil. A leackage of 5% of SF6 is assumed over the entire life cycle of the wind farm.\nThe modelled 1005 MW wind farm is a fictitious offshore wind farm based on the Renewable Energy Material Property Database, REMPD (Cooperman et al., 2023), consisting of 67 IEA reference offshore wind turbines with a nominal capacity of 15 MW and monopile substructures, as well as 1 offshore substation and 1 land-based substation..\nThe distance to service port is assumed to be 50 km. Total length of export cables is 210 km (assuming 3 parallel export cables of 70 km each). The total length of array cables is 133 km.\nThe model uses a capacity factor of 34.1%, representing the average capacity factor of offshore wind farms in Europe between 2016-2024 (source: ENTSO-E).\nAssumed lifetime is 25 years. Annual electricity production is 3004 GWh, applying a capacity factor of 34.1%.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
